## Working Conventions

### Required reading before implementation

**Read `docs/django.md` before starting any implementation.** It documents
installed apps, middleware order, settings conventions, admin patterns, and
migrations. It also indexes the focused docs below.

**Read `docs/conventions.md` before changing anything shared across files** —
version pins, environment variables, Redis databases, service names, or test settings.
It lists which files must change together. If another doc disagrees with it,
`docs/conventions.md` wins.

**Read `docs/this-project.md` and the `README.md` of any app you are changing.**
They describe this project's domain, business rules, APIs and integrations — the
context the generic docs below cannot give. If they contradict the code or are still
stubs, say so; `/djs-doc` creates and updates them.

**The backlog is the ordered work queue** (bugs, features, chores, with
blockers): GitHub issues when the project has a GitHub remote, otherwise
`docs/backlog.md`. `CHANGELOG.md` records user-visible changes. `/djs-backlog`
owns both: it keeps them current and picks up the next item. With any user-visible
change, add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry under `Unreleased` in the same commit (format:
`.agents/skills/djs-backlog/references/changelog-format.md`). Don't copy entries
from the django-studio template changelog that `/djs-sync` shows.

**Before starting any task, look up your task type in the table below and read
the listed doc(s) before writing any code.** The table is a lookup — use it
actively, not as background reading.

